      "id": 1,
      "text": "Johnsonburg was founded in 1810 when pioneer David Johnson settled at the confluence of the East and West Branches of the Clarion River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/johnsonburg_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town earned the nickname “Paper City” thanks to its long‑standing paper‑making industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitpago.com/counties/elk-county/johnsonburg-wilcox/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Railroad tracks arrived in the 1860s, spurring growth, a post office opened in 1888, and the borough incorporated in 1891.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/johnsonburg_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A Domtar paper mill still operates in Johnsonburg, a relic of the town’s once‑flourishing paper mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnsonburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1999 the Johnsonburg Commercial Historic District earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnsonburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
